    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "index": 13,
        "blockIndex": 10,
        "paragraphInBlock": 2,
        "text": "The triangle has a right angle at C, with AB as its hypotenuse and CB opposite the incidence angle at A, and sine means the opposite side length divided by the hypotenuse length.\nTogether with distance being speed multiplied by time, this gives:\n$|CB|=v_1\\cdot\\Delta t=|AB|\\sin\\alpha$ (7.1)."
      },
      {
        "index": 15,
        "blockIndex": 11,
        "paragraphInBlock": 1,
        "text": "This supplies the side-length relation for the second right triangle.\nIn this right triangle, AB is again the hypotenuse and AD is opposite the refraction angle at B, so:\n$|AD|=v_2\\cdot\\Delta t=|AB|\\sin\\beta$ (7.2)."
      }
    ],
