    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "index": 20,
        "blockIndex": 15,
        "paragraphInBlock": 0,
        "text": "Using relation (7.4), we can use the **absolute refractive indices** $n_1$ and $n_2$ of the first and second media to express the relative refractive index $n$.\nAn absolute refractive index uses light speed in a vacuum as its reference, with c denoting that vacuum speed, so for light of the same color the definitions are $n_1=\\frac{c}{v_1}$ and $n_2=\\frac{c}{v_2}$."
      }
    ],
